            <figcaption><b>Rebuilt</b> Remodeled from three reference views, by changing the script and re-running it.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <ul class="rb-changes">
          <li><b>Six</b> arched legs instead of four straight ones</li>
          <li><b>Knee wheels</b> and armored shins</li>
          <li><b>Two-talon</b> claws for feet</li>
          <li>A <b>jointed cannon</b> on a neck</li>
          <li><b>2× scale</b> after seeing it in the game</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <dl class="stats">
        <div><dt>910</dt><dd>lines in the vehicle script</dd></div>
        <div><dt>77k</dt><dd>triangles for the three tanks</dd></div>
        <div><dt>31.6k</dt><dd>triangles in the heavy walker</dd></div>
        <div><dt>2×</dt><dd>walker scale after the in-game check</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="block" id="testing">
      <p class="kicker">03 · Testing with a bot</p>
      <h2>A bot played every level, and its numbers decided what changed</h2>
      <p>The test bot plays whole levels through the real controls: it moves between cover, aims with human-like error and reaction time, fires in bursts, scans, throws detonators and calls in strikes. When it played too well I gave it an "average player" setting. Every 10 seconds it logs how many Umbarans are alive, its health, damage taken, kills, where it is on the road and the frame rate, and it photographs every key moment.</p>

      <div class="wide chart run">
        <h3>Level 3, the final run</h3>
        <p class="sub">Average-player bot on Medium. Shaded: Umbarans alive. Line: the bot's health. Bands mark each battle.</p>
        <div class="pwrap">
          <svg class="runchart" viewBox={`0 0 ${BW} ${BH}`} role="img" aria-label={`Level 3 bot run: ${fmt(bot.total)}, up to ${aMax} Umbarans alive at once, one death in battle 3`}>
            {bands.map((bd) => (
              <g>
                <rect x={bd.x0} y={by0} width={bd.x1 - bd.x0} height={by1 - by0} class="band" />
                <text x={bd.x0 + 6} y={by0 + 14} class="bl">Battle {bd.n}</text>
                <path d={`M${bd.taken} ${by0}V${by1}`} class="taken" />
